"prompt_steps":{"digest":"8452a1ae04f70067155bb051585fa52017159745f3f1e56f07869bb242918e86","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":11022},"state":{"digest":"409f6a17427a3cf67a01041164849d08a02af7f4a99945978f706a530da8f2a4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.1/state.json","size_bytes":183}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.1","local_name":"sase-qv.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-qv","agent_clan_generation":"20260819091530","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-qv.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-qv[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Required custom monitor statuses with deterministic pair colors[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every sase monitor declares its own running and finished status [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]labels, those labels are capped at 20 characters, and they appear [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]-- in one deterministic, pair-derived color -- on every surface [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that shows a monitor, including agent family container rows and the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Admin Center Procs tab.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]monitor_custom_statuses.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/monitor_custom_statuses.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-qv[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-qv/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor status contract module[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: add the shared sase.monitor_status module that owns the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default labels, the 20-character clamp, pair normalization, the 12-color[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accent palette, and the state-aware style rule; retire the scattered [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]MONITORING/MONITORED literals onto it.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required start and stop status flags[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: make -s/--start-status and -S/--stop-status required on sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor start, clamp over-length labels with a warning, make the two [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fields required on StartMonitorRequest, and render the effective label [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in sase monitor list, show, markdown, and JSON.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Status pair plumbing and terminality[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]model: carry monitor_stop_status alongside monitor_start_status through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the scan-wire and filesystem loaders, the TUI Agent row, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]RunningAgentInfo, the integrations entry, and the mobile summary; fix [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]settled monitors with custom stop labels being treated as non-terminal.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agents tab and agent list coloring[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]agents_tab[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents_tab: color the monitor status token by its pair accent in the ACE[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent list, add the outcome glyphs that replace the retired success [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]green, add a Status field to the prompt panel MONITOR section, and color[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase agent list STATUS badge.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agent family container status[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]family[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]family: mirror a monitor's custom status onto its agent family container[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row for plain families as well as plan roots, and copy the status pair [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so the mirrored row renders in the same accent as the monitor itself.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Procs tab monitor status chip[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]procs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]procs: resolve each monitor proc row's status pair from the loaded agent[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows and render the effective label as an accent-colored chip in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Admin Center Procs tab row labels and output header.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Guidance, skill, and docs[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]guidance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli, agents_tab[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guidance: teach TESTING/TESTED in the build-and-run memory note, make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase_monitor skill and monitors/ACE/CLI docs state that both flags [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]are required, and regenerate the derived instruction 